From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0001] ir: reject write_state whose value shape != state shape

mil_spec::ir validated dtype only when binding a value to write_state, so a
graph like `state kv: fp16[1,8,64,64]` + a [1,8,65,64] concat passed
compilation and produced a package coremlc rejected with:

  Unable to parse ML Program: in operation kv_write_state:
  Unexpected type for the data parameter.

A state is always written whole, so the value shape must equal the state's
declared shape. Two upstream fixtures had encoded the bug as correct
behaviour (tests/ir.rs::stateful_roundtrip and the mil_verify conformance
case "stateful-kv"); both are corrected to a legal whole-state write, and a
regression test asserts the rejection.

Upstream: 20f097fb34969cd577342a4d7996fbf5464998c8
--- a/src/ir.rs
+++ b/src/ir.rs
@@ -811,6 +811,21 @@
                 ),
             );
         }
+        // FORK(ane-stack): a state is written whole, so the value must match
+        // its declared shape exactly. Upstream checked dtype only, which let
+        // `state kv: fp16[1,8,64,64]` + a [1,8,65,64] concat through to
+        // coremlc, which then rejected the encoded program with
+        // "write_state: Unexpected type for the data parameter".
+        // Upstream: 20f097f.
+        if v.shape != st.shape {
+            return err(
+                n,
+                format!(
+                    "write_state shape mismatch: state {:?} vs value {:?}",
+                    st.shape, v.shape
+                ),
+            );
+        }
         self.block.write_state(parts[0], parts[1]);
         Ok(())
     }
